TC-09 manual evidence — Notifications and administration
Date: 2026-09-17

Administrator: phase2.manual-admin@fithub.test
Member: phase2.registration.20260916@fithub.test

Observed administration:
- Administrator dashboard displayed active members, active memberships, confirmed net revenue, payments today/month, trainer count, open faults, attendance trend, parking totals and equipment utilization.
- User management supported role/status search and account details.
- Administrator assigned Elena to Tariq; the active assignment retained who assigned it and when.
- The Trainer subsequently saw only the assigned Member.

Observed Member notifications:
- Personal record: New recorded best for Back Squat: 65 kg.
- Personal record: New recorded best for Bench Press: 42.5 kg.
- Fault report updated: Your report for Treadmill is now UnderReview.
- Each notification had a stable deduplication key in PostgreSQL.

Missing behaviour:
- No persisted notification-preference model/table or Member preference interface was found.
- Therefore notifications cannot be demonstrated as being sent according to the Member’s preferences, as required by FR-33.

Decision: FAIL
Reason: FR-35 and FR-36 were demonstrated, and deduplicated notifications exist, but FR-33 is only partial without preferences.
Defect: DEF-006 open.
